{"id": "EUVD-2026-101720", "enisaUuid": "09cc9722-f893-3b8d-b4e5-01787a555b66", "description": "FreeRDP 2.0.0 before 3.32.0, when built with WITH_LAME=ON and WITH_DSP_FFMPEG=OFF, has a heap-based buffer overflow in freerdp_dsp_decode_mp3 because the right-channel PCM pointer is offset by a byte count treated as short elements. A malicious RDP server can send MP3 audio over rdpsnd so decoded samples cross the heap allocation, crashing the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T13:47:43", "baseScore": 6.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-52xc-5973-w5vv", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-2.0.0-before-3.32.0-heap-buffer-overflow-via-mp3-audio-decoding"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110837", "GHSA-q3cv-4fpg-3hq2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fb654e3-56de-3752-95b2-1f62a6df2e20", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "566e498d-79ad-3475-8521-dbaf5f63eb87", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}